# Aethel Rules

These rules are the canonical project-wide constraints that every contributor
(human or AI) MUST honour. They are loaded by the Aethel chat via
`cloud-web-app/web/lib/server/project-rules.ts` and are also consumed natively
by Cursor / Windsurf / Copilot Workspace when the repo is opened there.

## Product Bar
- Optimize for the user-facing path first: `/`, `/dashboard`, `/ide`, `/docs`, billing, auth, preview.
- Prefer fewer, stronger surfaces over many shallow placeholders.
- If a route only redirects, implement it in `next.config.js` or middleware instead of shipping a stub page.

## Architecture
- Keep the canonical design system in `cloud-web-app/web/lib/design-tokens.ts` + CSS variables from `cloud-web-app/web/app/globals.css`.
- New UI primitives belong in `cloud-web-app/web/components/ui`.
- Collaboration primitives belong in `cloud-web-app/web/components/collaboration`.
- Avoid duplicate component names across folders. If a duplicate is unavoidable, document the canonical owner in `cloud-web-app/web/components/COMPONENT_CONSOLIDATION_MAP.md` first.
- Do not vendor third-party source trees into the main repo.
- Use project-relative paths only — never absolute OS paths (no `C:\…`, no `/home/…`).

## Quality
- No `console.log`, `console.info`, or `console.debug` in app code. Use `cloud-web-app/web/lib/observability/logger.ts` via `createComponentLogger('<module>')`.
- `console.warn` / `console.error` are allowed for framework-sensitive paths only.
- All new buttons must have an accessible name through text, `aria-label`, or `aria-labelledby`.
- Prefer request IDs, structured logs, and explicit error capture on server paths.
- Add or update tests when touching auth, billing, editor state, preview, or collaboration flows.
- No hard-coded hex colours in TSX (`bg-white`, `text-white`, etc.). Use design tokens (`var(--aethel-*)`) or the escape tokens `--aethel-text-inverse` / `--aethel-surface-contrast`.

## Observability
- Every server-side module must call `createComponentLogger(<name>)` once at the top and use `log.info` / `log.debug` / `log.warn` / `log.error`.
- Correlation IDs flow via the logger's `LogContext` — do not bypass the helper.

## Workbench
- The workbench is the product core. Favor `entry`-based convergence over parallel standalone shells.
- Split orchestration from panels and hooks before growing god-components further. The hard line is **500 lines per component file** before a refactor is non-negotiable.
- Collaboration features must degrade gracefully when realtime services are unavailable.
- Remote cursors, presence dots and collaborator avatars are implemented via `components/collaboration/*` + `hooks/useCollaborationAwareness`.

## Design system
- Theme toggling must respect `prefers-color-scheme` by default and honour `localStorage` overrides second.
- Every new component ships with at least one Storybook story under `components/**/*.stories.tsx`.
- QA gates that must stay green before merging:
  - `node tools/check-design-system-consistency.mjs` — 0 findings
  - `node tools/check-hardcoded-colors.mjs` — 0 findings
  - `node tools/check-button-types.mjs` — 0 findings

## Forbidden
- Reintroducing deleted dead libs (see `docs/master/80_DEAD_LIB_SWEEP.md` for the list).
- Absolute OS paths in source or documentation.
- `next.config.js` flags that disable Next/Image (`images.unoptimized: true`).
- `any` types in new code unless justified by a `// TODO(strict):` comment.

## Executor boot (Claude / Cursor agents)
- Open `docs/architecture/AETHEL_FOCUS1_EXECUTION_PROGRESS.md` then Master Map **current round only** — do not preload the full architecture corpus.
- Task queue = `AETHEL_CLAUDE_EXECUTION_MASTER_MAP.md`. Planning Completeness ≠ execution done.
- Order: Focus 1 → Focus 2 → Block 6. Import shipped libs; never reimplement Bridge / spend-resolver / heightfield.
- `cloud-web-app/CLAUDE_MASTER_EXECUTION_PLAN_V7|V8` and siblings are **SUPERSEDED** — ignore as DoD.
- Do not create new alignment MDs; annotate Index / Master Map / Progress.
